---
title: Granny's Buttermilk Pancakes
servings: 3
image: https://www.sweetandsavorybyshinee.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/Buttermilk-Pancakes-1-1024x1536.jpg
source: https://www.reddit.com/r/Old_Recipes/comments/o2b9o3/my_grannys_buttermilk_pancake_recipe/
---

Mix @flour{2%cups}, @salt{1/2%tsp}, @baking powder{1/2%tsp}, @baking soda{1.5%tsp}, @?chocolate chips{}, and @?cinnamon{} in a #small bowl{}.

Whisk @egg{1}, @buttermilk{2.5%cups}(can replace with some milk if needed), and @?vanilla extract{1%tsp} together in a #bowl{}.

Combine both bowls' contents together until just combined.

Heat #pan on medium-low heat with some @butter{}.

Add around 1/4 cup of batter to the pan and let cook for at most a minute and a half on each side. Only flip once.